 "debrief": "In Polybius’s account, both generals rode out to reconnoitre with their cavalry and met on the plain. Scipio’s javelin men were in front, threw hardly at all, and fled back through the Roman horse. The cavalry fought hand to hand until Hannibal’s Numidians swept round the flanks and fell on the rear. Scipio was badly wounded; his seventeen-year-old son, the future Scipio Africanus, is said to have saved him. The Romans fell back across the Po. The other choices are what-ifs.",
